# Protein Quest founder context

Act as Niketh Putta's business strategy + product engineering partner. Be concise, dense, and actionable. Never use em dashes. Always deploy web after UI/product changes the user can try (`npm run deploy:prod`). Prefer sharing https://proteinquest.vercel.app over proteinquest.app for app links.

## Founder

- **Name:** Niketh Putta (Instagram: niketh_putta)
- **Age:** 15 | **Based:** London
- **Prior win:** Grew an edtech SaaS to ~$2k MRR in a few months
- **Style:** Concise replies; no em dashes; deploy web after UI changes; prefer proteinquest.vercel.app links

## Mission

- Scale Protein Quest hard via influencer marketing
- Revenue goals: **$1k MRR**, then **$10k MRR** (aggressive summer timeline)
- **Private thesis (never put in user-facing product copy):** Prove influencer marketing can take a consumer app from zero to revenue. He may test even copied ideas. Mentors/partners get product + growth story, not "the app can be bad."

## Product: Protein Quest

- Gamified protein scanner/tracker: scan food, hit protein goal, feed/level a dragon
- **Pricing discussed:** £6.99/week or £29.99/month (yearly also on paywall)
- **Stack:** Expo / React Native, Supabase, Vercel web, RevenueCat / Stripe, EAS builds
- **Live web:** https://proteinquest.vercel.app (proteinquest.app is marketing/landing split)
- **Freemium:** `HABIT_GRACE_DAYS=2` (2-day unlimited trial), then `FREE_DAILY_SCANS=1` (soft paywall; keep **1**, not 0, unless he explicitly changes)
- **Scan UX:** camera square + optional user note fused with image for AI analyze-food; editable food name after scan; "Skip for now" on first scan; removed "No food handy" hint
- **Intro critical UX:** Dragon naming must never have CTA covering the name field (ScrollView + footer clearance on all screen sizes)
- **AI accuracy:** USDA/density grounding, expanded food tables (incl. Indian), portion-first prompts, note portion hints; keep costs reasonable (gpt-4o auto detail)

## Growth / marketing

- **Channel:** Instagram influencer marketing (CPM deals ~$1.50–$2.50 per 1k views discussed; pay-for-views painful when ROI bad)
- **Ops lesson:** Cap deals, track CPA not vanity views, pay agreed debts, don't ghost creators
- **Partnerships:** Co-founder/partner (e.g. Matty) only with **milestone vesting**, not 50% day one; he brings app, partner brings outreach machine. Trial before equity.
- **Mentors:** Affordable only (ADPList free, cold DM, ~$50 one-off), not $500/session celebrity coaches
- **Mentors of interest:** Jake Castillo (Cal AI), Alex Slater, Nicole Cheung, David Attias, Bhawna Sethi, Connor McLaren, etc.

## Shipping / stores

- Recent ship (commit e242b49 and earlier): scan UX, denser AI, 2-day trial, 1 free scan/day, intro/paywall fixes
- EAS production builds queued with auto-submit: Android `0a85031c` (v107), iOS `a8b3aab4` (build 35); submissions to Play production + App Store Connect
- Prefer: ship live web first for review; store builds only when explicitly requested
